{"title":"Career Roadmap · Clinical Dietitian","role":"Clinical Dietitian","summary":"A Clinical Dietitian applies nutrition science to the prevention and management of disease. The role involves nutritional assessment, diet planning, patient counselling, therapeutic nutrition, monitoring of nutritional outcomes, and collaboration with physicians, nurses, pharmacists and other healthcare professionals.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Dietitian applies nutrition science to the prevention and management of disease. The role involves nutritional assessment, diet planning, patient counselling, therapeutic nutrition, monitoring of nutritional outcomes, and collaboration with physicians, nurses, pharmacists and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the direct pathway within the supplied category is a recognized B.Sc/B.Sc (Hons.) Nutrition & Dietetics, Clinical Nutrition & Dietetics, Food & Nutrition, or equivalent nutrition/dietetics program, followed by any internship, registration or credentialing requirements applicable to the intended workplace. A generic BPT, BOT or BMLT degree does not automatically qualify a graduate as a Clinical Dietitian."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Dietitians commonly work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multispecialty hospitals"},{"text":"ICU and critical-care units"},{"text":"Diabetes centres"},{"text":"Renal clinics"},{"text":"Oncology centres"},{"text":"Gastroenterology departments"},{"text":"Paediatric hospitals"},{"text":"Sports and rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Long-term care facilities"},{"text":"Nutrition clinics"},{"text":"Public-health programs"},{"text":"Research and healthcare organizations"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Complete nutrition/dietetics education, clinical internship and develop therapeutic-diet competencies"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as Clinical Dietitian/Dietitian in hospitals or specialty clinics"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialize in critical care, renal, diabetes, oncology, paediatrics or another clinical area"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Clinical Dietitian, Clinical Nutrition Coordinator, Nutrition Services Manager, educator, researcher or specialist consultant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the UG Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Nutrition & Biomedical Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Build strong foundations in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Biological sciences"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Human biology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Nutrition science"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Macronutrients"},{"text":"Micronutrients"},{"text":"Energy metabolism"},{"text":"Digestion and absorption"},{"text":"Nutrient requirements"},{"text":"Dietary sources"},{"text":"Deficiency disorders"},{"text":"Nutrient interactions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Food science"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Food composition"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Food preservation"},{"text":"Food safety"},{"text":"Food microbiology"},{"text":"Food quality"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Nutrition Assessment & Diet Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop clinical nutrition fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Nutritional assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dietary history"},{"text":"Food-frequency assessment"},{"text":"24-hour dietary recall"},{"text":"Anthropometry"},{"text":"BMI"},{"text":"Weight trends"},{"text":"Biochemical indicators"},{"text":"Clinical signs and symptoms"}]},{"type":"h","text":